# Social Share Button Feature - Development Plan

## 📋 Executive Summary

Add a social media share button to product detail pages (PDP) that enables users to quickly share products on Facebook, Twitter, and LinkedIn. The button will be positioned below the product title section.

**Complexity Level:** MEDIUM  
**Estimated Effort:** 2-3 hours  
**Risk Level:** LOW (no external dependencies, vanilla JS)

---

## 🎯 Objectives & Requirements

### Functional Requirements

1. **Display Social Share Buttons** on PDP below product title
   - Facebook
   - Twitter
   - LinkedIn
   - Fallback to Web Share API for mobile/native share

2. **Share Functionality**
   - Pre-fill with product name and product URL
   - Each platform opens native share dialog
   - No server-side tracking required initially

3. **User Experience**
   - Display as inline button group with social platform icons
   - Responsive design (mobile-first)
   - Accessible keyboard navigation
   - Clear visual feedback on hover/focus

### Technical Requirements

1. **Architecture Pattern**
   - Follow existing block decorator pattern
   - Use vanilla JavaScript (NO external dependencies)
   - Use native DOM elements (`document.createElement()`)
   - No Preact/VNode usage
   - Compatible with AEM EDS

2. **Integration Point**
   - Integrate into existing `product-details.js` block
   - Positioned after `ProductHeader` container
   - Access product name and URL from page context

3. **Browser Compatibility**
   - Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)
   - Graceful fallback if APIs unavailable
   - Mobile-friendly (responsive)

---

## 🏗️ Architecture & Design

### Approach: Integrated Into Product Details Block

**Why:** 
- Product detail page already renders product title and metadata
- Keeps social share feature cohesive with product context
- Avoids creating separate isolated block
- Simpler integration and maintenance

### Component Structure

```
product-details.js (existing)
├── Renders ProductHeader (title)
└── NEW: Renders SocialShare component
    ├── Facebook share button
    ├── Twitter share button
    ├── LinkedIn share button
    └── Web Share fallback

product-details.css (existing)
└── NEW: Social share styling

social-share.js (NEW - utility module)
└── Reusable social share logic
```

### Data Requirements

- **Product Name:** From `ProductHeader` or PDP data payload
- **Product URL:** `window.location.href` or from page metadata
- **Product Image:** Optional, for social preview (use product image if available)

### Layout Design

```
┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│    Product Title/Header         │
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│  [f] [𝕏] [in]  Social Share    │  ← NEW
├─────────────────────────────────┤
│    Price, Options, etc.         │
```

---

## 📋 Implementation Roadmap

### Phase 1: Create Social Share Utility Module

**File:** `blocks/product-details/social-share.js`

Exports:
- `createSocialShareButtons(productName, productUrl, productImage)`
- Returns DOM element with social buttons

Features:
- Create button container
- Add Facebook share button with share URL
- Add Twitter share button with tweet text
- Add LinkedIn share button
- Add native share fallback
- Attach click handlers

### Phase 2: Integrate Into Product Details

**File:** `blocks/product-details/product-details.js`

Changes:
- Import social-share utility
- After ProductHeader is rendered, insert social share buttons
- Pass product name and URL to social share creator

### Phase 3: Style Social Share Component

**File:** `blocks/product-details/product-details.css`

New Classes:
- `.product-details__social-share` - Container
- `.product-details__social-share__button` - Individual button
- `.product-details__social-share__button--facebook`
- `.product-details__social-share__button--twitter`
- `.product-details__social-share__button--linkedin`
- `.product-details__social-share__button--native` - Web Share API fallback

Styling:
- Inline flex layout (horizontal button group)
- Icon-based buttons with hover states
- Responsive padding/sizing
- Accessibility focus states
- Color scheme matching brand

### Phase 4: Testing & Validation

**Test Scenarios:**
1. Verify buttons render on PDP
2. Test each social platform opens correct share dialog
3. Verify product name and URL are passed correctly
4. Test on mobile devices (Web Share fallback)
5. Test keyboard navigation (Tab, Enter)
6. Test with screen readers
7. Responsive design (mobile 375px, tablet 768px, desktop 1024px+)
8. Test with different product types (simple, configurable, etc.)

---

## 🔍 Technical Deep Dive

### Social Share URLs

**Facebook:**
```
https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u={productUrl}
```

**Twitter:**
```
https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url={productUrl}&text={productName}
```

**LinkedIn:**
```
https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url={productUrl}
```

**Web Share API (Native):**
```javascript
navigator.share({
  title: productName,
  url: productUrl,
  text: 'Check out this product!'
})
```

### Implementation Code Pattern

```javascript
// Create button
const button = document.createElement('button');
button.className = 'product-details__social-share__button product-details__social-share__button--facebook';
button.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Share on Facebook');
button.innerHTML = '<span class="icon">f</span>'; // or actual icon

// Attach handler
button.addEventListener('click', () => {
  const shareUrl = `https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=${encodeURIComponent(productUrl)}`;
  window.open(shareUrl, 'facebook-share', 'width=600,height=400');
});

// Append to container
container.appendChild(button);
```

### Extract Product Data

From existing PDP data flow:
```javascript
// Get from page
const productName = document.querySelector('.product-title')?.textContent || 'Check out this product';
const productUrl = window.location.href;

// Or from event payload (if available)
const product = events.lastPayload('pdp/data');
```

